ly observable effect a message."] [192 1 "// ioManagerAvailable is parseIOManagerFlag's answer: available, unavailable, or unrecognised."] [213 1 "// procRtsOpts reads the options args (the RTS's, in order: -with-rtsopts', then the command line's); a refusal panics"] [214 1 "// with rtsExit after its messages."] [339 13 "// getNumberOfProcessors: hsi has one capability's processor"] [374 4 "// openStatsFile: a file name opens the file; the statistics hsi does not have are not written"] [411 39 "// -N: the processors' count (getNumberOfProcessors)"] [507 1 "// splitRtsFlags is the RTS's splitting of -with-rtsopts' string into options (at spaces and tabs)."] [510 1 "// run reads the options: false with the status when they end the run."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[75 17] [75 24] [76 46] [146 48] [181 12] [181 26] [237 93] [238 95] [239 95] [261 28] [273 39] [396 38] [404 33] [513 20]]} (go/file "rtsflags.go" :imports [

