    ;; option accepted or refused with the RTS's message, an error ending the run as errorUsage ends it (each message and the
    ;; usage text by errorBelch, status 1). Of the values, hsi uses -K (the stack's limit) and -xq (the allocation limit's
    ;; grace); the others have no meaning in hsi (heap and GC sizes, the eventlog, statistics files: -s, -S and -t's statistics
    ;; are not printed).


